},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dmn7g","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"87com","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Beautiful home grown Bartlett Pears","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"5a21q","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_3470c1c846c944d4adc646bd3336dc97~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Home Grown Bartlett Pears"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cpeua","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"27mk9","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" We have a very old pear tree that never ceases to amaze us. It's producing wonderful fruit every year with very little attention other than it gets watered when we water the lawn. We always have one bug in each pear but they don't eat much and I cut away that part. We have more fruit than we can use every year. I've made juice and canned pears and made many delicious deserts like ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Pear Blackberry Crisp","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"#0957a2"}},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true},{"type":"LINK","linkData":{"link":{"url":"www.theglasspantry.com/single-post/2017/09/03/Pear-Blackberry-Crisp","target":"BLANK"}}}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" and we still can't use them up.  Usually we give away a few boxes to friends and lots drop off the tree for our dog Jolie to eat. Years ago we had an old dog named Jake who also liked to help clean up the extra pears. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"2v2b3","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4m0ij","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dimmn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bk114","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"GALLERY","id":"70e5q","nodes":[],"galleryData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"items":[{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_e12fc800b5b24e4f8c196a75abc52777~mv2_d_3024_4032_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":3024,"height":4032}},"title":"calibrachoe and winter savory"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_bf20240a51594aca85eeb7ceea9a542a~mv2_d_3024_4032_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":3024,"height":4032}},"title":"Cordyline, Petunias and Sage"}],"options":{"layout":{"type":"GRID","horizontalScroll":false,"orientation":"ROWS","numberOfColumns":2},"item":{"targetSize":300,"ratio":1,"crop":"FILL","spacing":10},"thumbnails":{"placement":"BOTTOM","spacing":0}}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"agp0g","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"The pretty pink calibrachoa I started from seeds I saved last year. It's super easy to do. I wait until the plant has gone completely dormant and the branches have dried on the plant, then I cut the branches and store them in plastic produce bags in a dark cupboard for the winter. In the spring, I shake the dry branches in whatever pot I want the calibrachoe to grow in and they grow! I'm going to try to get them going somewhere as ground cover next spring.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bm3ls","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"92pje","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"The winter savory above on the left is very invasive in our climate so I keep it in 2 pots that I have and one small space near the barn. It looks a little like rosemary but produces tiny white flowers along it's branches that the honey bees love. I use the herb dried or fresh in dishes where I would use sage or thyme. It's great on meats and roasted veggies.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5l5gg","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"49fld","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I sent the spikey cordyline (above right) home with my step son to Portland so it would live. It will look great at his house by the pool! I think the sage  and petunias might make it on the front porch out of the wind for the winter. Petunias don't really make it through the winter here but they are good re-seeders.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"72fqk","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignmen